go-ethereum (github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum)
    Library packages used: accounts/keystore, common, core, core/forkid,
    core/types, crypto, log, p2p, p2p/discover, p2p/dnsdisc, p2p/enode, p2p/enr,
    p2p/netutil, p2p/rlpx, params, rlp.
    Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 (LGPL-3.0).
    LGPL-3.0 permits use within this AGPL-3.0 work. Users are entitled to the
    relinking rights the LGPL provides; build instructions are in the README so a
    modified version of the linked library may be substituted.
    No code was copied from go-ethereum's GPL-3.0 `cmd/` tooling.

MaxMind GeoLite2
    This product includes GeoLite2 data created by MaxMind, available from
    https://www.maxmind.com. Use is subject to the GeoLite2 End User License
    Agreement. GeoLite2 databases are not distributed with this repository; they are
    fetched at deploy time using an operator-supplied license key.

go-libp2p (github.com/libp2p/go-libp2p)
    Used to probe consensus-layer (beacon) nodes over libp2p and read the
    identify AgentVersion. MIT licensed.

DuckDB and duckdb-go (github.com/duckdb/duckdb-go)
    DuckDB is embedded by the API query engine through its official Go bindings.
    MIT licensed. Copyright the DuckDB Foundation and contributors.

MinIO Go client (github.com/minio/minio-go)
    S3-compatible object storage client. Apache License 2.0.

Prometheus Go client (github.com/prometheus/client_golang)
    Metrics exposition and collectors. Apache License 2.0.

AWS SDK for Go v2 (github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2)
    Route53 client used by the DNS tree publisher. Apache License 2.0.

go-git (github.com/go-git/go-git/v5)
    Pure-Go git client used by the DNS tree publisher's git output. Apache License 2.0.
    Notable transitives: go-billy (Apache-2.0), ProtonMail/go-crypto (BSD-3-Clause),
    skeema/knownhosts (Apache-2.0), kevinburke/ssh_config (MIT), sergi/go-diff (MIT),
    emirpasic/gods (BSD-2-Clause).

parquet-go (github.com/parquet-go/parquet-go)
    Snapshot serialization. Apache License 2.0.

React, deck.gl, and their supporting web packages
    Used by the static explorer under permissive licenses. Exact package names and
    versions are recorded in web/package-lock.json.
